SOLR-4960: fix race in CoreContainer.getCore

git-svn-id: https://svn.apache.org/repos/asf/lucene/dev/trunk@1496620 13f79535-47bb-0310-9956-ffa450edef68

Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by a race condition in the `CoreContainer` class, where a request could attempt to use a core that had already been shut down. This occurred because the method `getCoreFromAnyList` did not properly manage the reference count of the cores, allowing a core to be closed while still being accessed by another thread. The modifications introduced a mechanism to increment the reference count when retrieving cores, ensuring that a core remains open while it is being used, thus preventing access to a shut-down core.

